1
00:00:09,809 --> 00:00:11,845
Don't tell anyone
what I'm about to tell you.

2
00:00:24,391 --> 00:00:26,526
Can you tell me your story?

3
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:30,764
The security camera footage with me on it…

4
00:00:32,432 --> 00:00:34,267
Who in the police has seen it?

5
00:00:34,334 --> 00:00:35,435
Your story first.

6
00:00:35,502 --> 00:00:36,736
I'll ask again.

7
00:00:38,605 --> 00:00:40,607
-Who saw it?
-You first--

8
00:00:40,673 --> 00:00:43,343
We don't intend to harm you.

9
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,677
Please put this on.

10
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:45,812
A blindfold?

11
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:46,913
If you please.

12
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,217
Please get in.

13
00:00:52,118 --> 00:00:53,153
-Yes.
-Really?

14
00:00:53,686 --> 00:00:55,455
-Let's go.
-Hang on.

15
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:57,490
For real?

16
00:01:08,201 --> 00:01:09,803
Maybe one of you should go home.

17
00:01:09,869 --> 00:01:12,305
No, I can't leave after coming this far.

18
00:01:12,372 --> 00:01:15,008
You're looking for Harune Nikaido,
right, insurance man?

19
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,043
I'm not an "insurance man."
I'm an investigator!

20
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,112
Please identify yourselves as well.

21
00:01:19,179 --> 00:01:20,713
You're not office workers, right?

22
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,918
It would help a lot if you told us
where Harune is and what she's doing.

23
00:01:27,554 --> 00:01:29,089
Huh? Did time stop?

24
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:33,493
Mr. Monden, are you police?

25
00:01:34,627 --> 00:01:36,663
From your eyes and the way you moved.

26
00:01:36,729 --> 00:01:38,665
I figured you must be police.

27
00:01:38,731 --> 00:01:40,166
Which department?

28
00:01:45,505 --> 00:01:47,841
Hokkaido Police HQ,
Organized Crime Division.

29
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,409
What?

30
00:01:49,476 --> 00:01:53,012
-So everyone here is Hokkaido police?
-No.

31
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:56,583
She's from the Hokkaido Bureau of Health,
Narcotics Control. A narcotics agent.

32
00:01:56,649 --> 00:02:00,120
And I'm with Hakodate Customs
Anti-Smuggling Department.

33
00:02:00,186 --> 00:02:05,058
So, police, narcotics, customs.

34
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,227
Is this a joint operation?

35
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,928
That is correct.

36
00:02:09,562 --> 00:02:12,065
-Show me your IDs.
-Now's not the time.

37
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:14,501
They sound fishy.
This could be a kind of scam.

38
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:15,568
Give me your phone.

39
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:16,469
Huh?

40
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:18,204
Don't "huh" me. Your phone.

41
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:23,710
Here.

42
00:02:24,677 --> 00:02:25,345
You too.

43
00:02:28,781 --> 00:02:30,483
But if anything happens to me,

44
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:34,287
my Tokyo investigation report
is set to be sent to my station,

45
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:36,723
along with the CCTV footage.

46
00:02:38,291 --> 00:02:40,827
I don't know what happened
on that mountain…

47
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:42,495
-Undo those settings.
-Do it!

48
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:45,732
I'll undo it once I know
why you're gathered here.

49
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:48,635
Okay, okay! Stop!

50
00:02:48,701 --> 00:02:51,237
Our identities are genuine!

51
00:02:52,438 --> 00:02:55,808
We're investigating a certain drug case.

52
00:02:56,876 --> 00:02:59,078
We were tracking Motoka Tabatake.

53
00:03:01,748 --> 00:03:03,349
Since we're on a drug case,

54
00:03:03,416 --> 00:03:06,319
shouldn't we minimize
the risk of information leakage?

55
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:09,088
Mr. Ogoma aside,
do we need to let Mr. Nao hear this?

56
00:03:09,155 --> 00:03:12,292
Because of my job, I bet I'm the best
secret keeper around here.

57
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:14,961
I've cooperated with police
investigations many times.

58
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:17,130
The investigation of this case--

59
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:18,865
-Whoa!
-Hey, you okay?

60
00:03:18,932 --> 00:03:20,466
Such a pain. Just leave.

61
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,001
What era is he from?

62
00:03:22,068 --> 00:03:24,304
-You're the one who got caught!
-What?!

63
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,873
-You stand out too much!
-I know that.

64
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,841
Wait, aren't you two married?

65
00:03:28,908 --> 00:03:30,310
No!

66
00:03:33,179 --> 00:03:35,348
Can I start explaining?

67
00:03:36,082 --> 00:03:37,417
Do you need the restroom first?

68
00:03:37,483 --> 00:03:38,685
I'll go quickly.

69
00:03:38,751 --> 00:03:41,087
-Go ahead.
-Please start. Hold it in.

70
00:03:41,154 --> 00:03:42,155
How long will it take?

71
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:43,856
Six months ago,

72
00:03:43,923 --> 00:03:47,894
a neighboring country sent information
to Hakodate Customs.

73
00:03:47,961 --> 00:03:51,364
About a certain product
being sent to Japan regularly.

74
00:03:51,431 --> 00:03:55,201
It contains an essential ingredient
for making banned drugs.

75
00:03:55,268 --> 00:03:56,302
What product?

76
00:03:56,369 --> 00:03:57,804
Which neighboring country?

77
00:03:57,870 --> 00:04:00,573
We are only telling you what we can.

78
00:04:01,107 --> 00:04:05,078
Dangerous things entering from overseas
must be stopped at all costs.

79
00:04:05,144 --> 00:04:09,916
If they are used for criminal purposes,
it will be Customs' responsibility.

80
00:04:09,983 --> 00:04:15,922
We confirmed that Tabatake herself
received the package we were tipped about.

81
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:21,761
Yes, she received it.

82
00:04:21,828 --> 00:04:25,398
Of course, we also checked
the contents ourselves.

83
00:04:25,465 --> 00:04:30,036
Customs has investigative authority
but no arrest powers,

84
00:04:32,071 --> 00:04:34,641
so we asked Narcotics and the police…

85
00:04:36,242 --> 00:04:38,011
We joined the investigation.

86
00:04:38,645 --> 00:04:39,679
You tell the rest.

87
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:46,986
Tabatake has no prior record
in drug smuggling.

88
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:52,091
We figured she couldn't be the endpoint,
but just a courier.

89
00:04:52,158 --> 00:04:54,460
So we monitored where the package went.

90
00:04:54,994 --> 00:04:55,895
A courier?

91
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:56,863
I love you.

92
00:04:56,929 --> 00:04:57,964
I love you.

93
00:04:58,031 --> 00:05:01,334
Tabatake received the package,

94
00:05:01,401 --> 00:05:04,704
carried it somewhere,
and handed it to someone.

95
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,808
Finding the delivery destination
was difficult.

96
00:05:08,875 --> 00:05:12,178
As a mountain guide and a driver,

97
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:15,281
she went all over Hokkaido.

98
00:05:15,915 --> 00:05:22,588
But we noticed a pattern in her actions
the day after a package was delivered.

99
00:05:23,556 --> 00:05:26,125
She always climbed Mt. Shikara.

100
00:05:26,192 --> 00:05:29,262
She carried a rather heavy pack
for a day trip.

101
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:33,633
In town, we could monitor her,
but in the mountains, it's difficult.

102
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:37,937
So we posed as tour guests
to watch Tabatake's movements.

103
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:40,506
And find out where the goods went.

104
00:05:41,274 --> 00:05:43,276
That was the only way.

105
00:05:43,976 --> 00:05:47,480
For a courier, Tabatake lacked wariness.

106
00:05:47,547 --> 00:05:51,517
Ms. Saruwatari, you've climbed
this mountain several times, right?

107
00:05:51,584 --> 00:05:52,485
Yes.

108
00:05:52,552 --> 00:05:55,955
"Maybe she isn't carrying
the goods today."

109
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:59,525
"Today's operation might come to nothing."

110
00:05:59,592 --> 00:06:01,994
Those were the worries we had.

111
00:06:03,896 --> 00:06:05,064
Mr. Tsugaru?

112
00:06:05,832 --> 00:06:07,033
No.

113
00:06:10,436 --> 00:06:11,771
Tsugaru.

114
00:06:11,838 --> 00:06:14,540
Tabatake's breathing changed.

115
00:06:14,607 --> 00:06:16,075
She was wary of Nikaido.

116
00:06:16,142 --> 00:06:17,610
Ring this up please.

117
00:06:17,677 --> 00:06:21,647
Tabatake called Nikaido "Tsugaru," right?

118
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:22,749
That's correct.

119
00:06:22,815 --> 00:06:24,951
They clearly knew each other.

120
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:28,821
However,
Nikaido was not on Tabatake's friend list

121
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:34,160
or her contact list,
so we didn't know who he was.

122
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:36,028
Hey, can you take a photo of me?

123
00:06:36,095 --> 00:06:37,397
-Is here okay?
-Yes!

124
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,235
Here I go.

125
00:06:42,301 --> 00:06:43,202
Okay.

126
00:06:43,269 --> 00:06:45,738
When we asked the police headquarters,

127
00:06:45,805 --> 00:06:49,242
we learned he was a man
running a restaurant in Asahikawa.

128
00:06:49,308 --> 00:06:52,145
If the police know him,

129
00:06:52,211 --> 00:06:54,781
does that mean
Nikaido had a criminal record?

130
00:06:55,448 --> 00:06:58,317
No, he was a witness in a fraud case.

131
00:06:58,384 --> 00:06:59,352
A witness?

132
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:02,288
We are only telling you what we can.

133
00:07:02,355 --> 00:07:07,360
Nikaido didn't use his real name
and approached Tabatake under a false one.

134
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:10,863
We believed there must be a reason,

135
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,900
and so we watched their actions
and conversations closely.

136
00:07:13,966 --> 00:07:16,769
-The pixie-eye primrose.
-I see.

137
00:07:16,836 --> 00:07:19,439
It's common sense
to take trash home with you.

138
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:24,343
Mr. Nikaido.

139
00:07:24,410 --> 00:07:27,713
The package delivered to Tabatake
weighed two kilograms.

140
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,416
If she secretly took it
out of her backpack,

141
00:07:30,483 --> 00:07:32,785
we could tell
by how her steps got lighter.

142
00:07:32,852 --> 00:07:35,221
And that would be
where she left the goods.

143
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:38,925
Why did Nikaido join the tour?

144
00:07:38,991 --> 00:07:42,094
Why did he approach Tabatake?

145
00:07:42,595 --> 00:07:43,729
We don't know yet.

146
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,798
There is something
I would like to show you.

147
00:07:47,099 --> 00:07:50,570
None of us could predict
that there would be such a thunderstorm.

148
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:54,140
Mr. Monden! Misaki!

149
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:56,909
Mr. Uematsu! Are you hurt?

150
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:59,479
I'm okay!

151
00:07:59,545 --> 00:08:00,746
I'm going home.

152
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:01,647
Don't move!

153
00:08:01,714 --> 00:08:03,583
I'm cold. A bath…

154
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:06,319
-Mr. Nikaido!
-I want to take a bath!

155
00:08:06,385 --> 00:08:07,620
Mr. Nikaido!

156
00:08:07,687 --> 00:08:09,088
Mr. Nikaido!

157
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:11,724
-It's dangerous!
-Are you all right?

158
00:08:11,791 --> 00:08:14,560
-Please stay here!
-Hey!

159
00:08:14,627 --> 00:08:15,828
Help me, you moron!

160
00:08:15,895 --> 00:08:19,765
We couldn't follow Tabatake and Nikaido.

161
00:08:20,366 --> 00:08:21,734
They got away from us.

162
00:08:21,801 --> 00:08:24,470
Who chased Nikaido when he went down?

163
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:25,938
Tabatake.

164
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:29,542
About an hour later,
Saruwatari also went down to seek help.

165
00:08:30,076 --> 00:08:33,312
And then one died, and two went missing.

166
00:08:33,379 --> 00:08:37,149
Even with bad weather,
we have to admit the operation failed.

167
00:08:37,216 --> 00:08:38,951
-We found a personal item.
-Thanks!

168
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,753
-We're going home.
-See you tomorrow.

169
00:08:42,989 --> 00:08:46,425
Who in the police knows
you were investigating a drug case?

170
00:08:46,492 --> 00:08:48,995
Only the bare minimum.

171
00:08:49,061 --> 00:08:50,496
The rescue team…

172
00:08:50,563 --> 00:08:52,565
Do you know how hard
they searched for you?!

173
00:08:52,632 --> 00:08:54,767
The search was called off four days ago.

174
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,537
And Tabatake, whom we rescued…

175
00:08:58,838 --> 00:08:59,705
She died.

176
00:08:59,772 --> 00:09:01,674
Whose fault do you think that was?!

177
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:04,544
She jumped when you looked away?

178
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:07,380
You useless small-town police
ruined our investigation!

179
00:09:07,446 --> 00:09:09,115
How will you take responsibility?

180
00:09:09,181 --> 00:09:10,116
Well?

181
00:09:12,585 --> 00:09:15,688
Saruwatari is suspected of murder.

182
00:09:17,757 --> 00:09:21,494
Saruwatari or Tabatake?
Who handed him the water?

183
00:09:24,797 --> 00:09:28,200
Ms. Saruwatari, I have a spare bottle.

184
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:30,002
Take it to Mr. Nikaido.

185
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:31,504
Yes.

186
00:09:33,539 --> 00:09:35,408
What? Yes, like that.

187
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:39,345
-Can you get it off?
-Yes.

188
00:09:43,983 --> 00:09:47,720
So you say Saruwatari
handed over Tabatake's water?

189
00:09:47,787 --> 00:09:50,756
Her testimony was consistent
with the truth.

190
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:56,128
Do you believe Tabatake
intended to kill him?

191
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,497
That's hard to say.

192
00:09:59,065 --> 00:10:01,067
Just tell us your subjective opinion.

193
00:10:05,237 --> 00:10:08,341
She didn't look like
she was trying to kill him.

194
00:10:10,142 --> 00:10:13,646
This fact was never shared
with our investigation team.

195
00:10:15,014 --> 00:10:16,148
You're right.

196
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:20,252
Do you know
what situation Saruwatari is in?

197
00:10:20,319 --> 00:10:23,122
Every day, she is accused of murder,

198
00:10:23,189 --> 00:10:25,992
she denies it,
yet the police don't believe her at all!

199
00:10:27,326 --> 00:10:29,362
If you could testify in her favor…

200
00:10:29,428 --> 00:10:32,131
We can't share what we saw and learned

201
00:10:32,198 --> 00:10:35,835
with an unspecified number
of investigators.

202
00:10:35,901 --> 00:10:38,704
Our investigation is secret
within our own agencies.

203
00:10:38,771 --> 00:10:41,240
How can I prove Saruwatari's innocence?

204
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:43,309
How many times do I have to say it?

205
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:47,647
You live deep in the mountains,
so you may not have seen or heard of it.

206
00:10:48,214 --> 00:10:50,983
Last year, a highly lethal drug

207
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:55,254
was widely circulated in Sapporo,
Hakodate, Tokyo, and Kanagawa.

208
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,057
It goes by the name "CAN-d."

209
00:10:58,124 --> 00:11:00,359
Its addictiveness rivals fentanyl.

210
00:11:00,426 --> 00:11:02,828
Many users die of an overdose.

211
00:11:02,895 --> 00:11:05,231
They can't control their actions.

212
00:11:05,297 --> 00:11:07,233
What Tabatake carried

213
00:11:07,299 --> 00:11:09,835
was an ingredient used
as a raw material for CAN-d.

214
00:11:09,902 --> 00:11:13,239
Before it is manufactured
and circulated again,

215
00:11:13,305 --> 00:11:18,177
we must root it out at the source,
or lives and futures will be ruined.

216
00:11:18,244 --> 00:11:19,445
That must not happen.

217
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:22,515
Between Saruwatari,
who is only suspected of murder,

218
00:11:22,581 --> 00:11:26,218
and the many people
who will die if we fail,

219
00:11:27,286 --> 00:11:28,788
which matters more?

220
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:35,695
It's not about who matters more or less!

221
00:11:38,664 --> 00:11:42,401
You are okay with letting
an innocent person take the blame?

222
00:11:45,671 --> 00:11:50,109
If that's allowed,
what are we police even for?

223
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:57,750
I'm an amateur,
so it's not my place to interrupt.

224
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:01,921
But just being suspected of murder

225
00:12:03,022 --> 00:12:06,092
can ruin a person's life.

226
00:12:07,326 --> 00:12:09,395
Ms. Saruwatari is a teacher.

227
00:12:10,196 --> 00:12:14,600
Like all of you, her job requires trust,
first and foremost.

228
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:18,604
I ask that you show
the slightest bit of decency.

229
00:12:22,475 --> 00:12:23,676
Please.

230
00:12:26,378 --> 00:12:27,480
I'll take you home.

231
00:12:27,546 --> 00:12:29,515
Could you answer my question?

232
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:30,449
What?

233
00:12:31,350 --> 00:12:33,986
Where did Harune go?

234
00:12:39,892 --> 00:12:44,964
The fact that the three of you
are in Tokyo…

235
00:12:45,865 --> 00:12:47,566
means you haven't found her yet.

236
00:12:47,633 --> 00:12:49,368
Or you're keeping her under surveillance.

237
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:52,471
Two options. Which is it?

238
00:12:53,506 --> 00:12:57,977
Well, we have also gathered
some information--

239
00:12:58,043 --> 00:12:58,978
That hurts!

240
00:12:59,044 --> 00:13:00,379
We don't need it.

241
00:13:01,313 --> 00:13:03,115
I haven't said anything yet!

242
00:13:05,184 --> 00:13:06,218
Sorry.

243
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:07,753
Don't report what you've found.

244
00:13:08,821 --> 00:13:09,789
Undo the setting.

245
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:22,701
Just quietly go back to your small town.

246
00:13:25,037 --> 00:13:25,871
Hey!

247
00:13:25,938 --> 00:13:28,340
You, take them out of here.

248
00:13:44,123 --> 00:13:45,391
You understand, right?

249
00:13:45,457 --> 00:13:48,661
We understand.
We won't tell anyone. Right?

250
00:13:55,601 --> 00:13:57,603
Idiot!

251
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,305
He can't hear you.

252
00:14:01,774 --> 00:14:02,842
Your flight back.

253
00:14:03,409 --> 00:14:04,443
Will you make it?

254
00:14:06,212 --> 00:14:07,546
I still have time.

255
00:14:09,448 --> 00:14:11,450
Then let's have coffee.

256
00:14:13,285 --> 00:14:15,120
Ogoma, you should try shouting it too.

257
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:16,789
-Idiot!
-Idiot!

258
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:21,026
Again, I'm surprised how gutsy you are.

259
00:14:21,093 --> 00:14:23,429
You did well, sticking with me.

260
00:14:24,496 --> 00:14:28,434
I thought I would get kidnapped again.
I was ready to die.

261
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:29,702
Thank you for waiting.

262
00:14:29,768 --> 00:14:31,437
Thank you. Here.

263
00:14:31,503 --> 00:14:32,872
Thank you.

264
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:37,309
If this is a contest,
it feels like we've lost, right?

265
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:40,779
Yes, we lost.

266
00:14:43,515 --> 00:14:46,518
But Ms. Aya's testimony wasn't a lie.

267
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:51,257
You grasped the truth
and also stood up for what's important.

268
00:14:51,323 --> 00:14:52,691
Not bad.

269
00:14:54,159 --> 00:14:55,327
Thanks.

270
00:14:56,762 --> 00:14:59,365
I couldn't ask even
half the things I wanted.

271
00:15:00,332 --> 00:15:03,702
Why did Ms. Tabatake hand water
to Nikaido, of all people?

272
00:15:06,939 --> 00:15:07,940
Let's…

273
00:15:09,141 --> 00:15:10,509
take a break from thinking.

274
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:15,214
Ms. Tabatake…

275
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:18,951
Maybe she didn't know
about the sleeping pills in the bottle.

276
00:15:19,618 --> 00:15:21,553
Is that possible?

277
00:15:22,488 --> 00:15:23,389
Well…

278
00:15:23,455 --> 00:15:27,159
The customs man said he couldn't tell
whether she had intent to kill.

279
00:15:27,226 --> 00:15:30,195
But the beneficiary on the hiking
insurance was rewritten, right?

280
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:32,865
Maybe she was trying
to cast suspicion on Ms. Aya.

281
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:35,668
I wonder.

282
00:15:37,169 --> 00:15:42,975
Maybe Ms. Tabatake
thought Nikaido would harm her.

283
00:15:44,243 --> 00:15:48,013
If a tragedy happened on the mountain
and the insurance looked suspicious,

284
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,649
the police would start investigating.

285
00:15:52,151 --> 00:15:57,589
Maybe she rewrote
the beneficiary's name as an SOS.

286
00:15:57,656 --> 00:15:59,692
You're really defending Tabatake.

287
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,495
I think it's true she was a courier.

288
00:16:03,562 --> 00:16:07,099
But the Narcotics woman
said she carried an ingredient.

289
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,935
She didn't say she carried drugs.

290
00:16:11,236 --> 00:16:17,142
If what she carried wasn't illegal,
we can't say she is a criminal.

291
00:16:17,209 --> 00:16:21,080
If she were a criminal,
what happens to her life insurance money?

292
00:16:22,047 --> 00:16:23,782
I can't say anything for now.

293
00:16:23,849 --> 00:16:25,117
Say it.

294
00:16:27,286 --> 00:16:29,355
There are cases where it isn't paid.

295
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:36,228
You want Nono to get it, right?

296
00:16:36,295 --> 00:16:38,297
No. I want to get my fee.

297
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:42,468
If the insurance is paid,
I get a commission.

298
00:16:44,603 --> 00:16:46,505
Do you really just want money?

299
00:16:48,774 --> 00:16:53,178
If she is only suspected,
the life insurance should be paid in full.

300
00:16:53,746 --> 00:16:56,815
It's the policyholder's
and beneficiary's right.

301
00:16:58,384 --> 00:17:02,354
It's sad for Nono,
but a criminal is usually penalized.

302
00:17:02,421 --> 00:17:05,657
You say that
because you're a police officer. I am--

303
00:17:05,724 --> 00:17:08,994
An insurance investigator,
so you think in money.

304
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:12,364
We don't…

305
00:17:12,431 --> 00:17:13,832
See things the same way.

306
00:17:19,238 --> 00:17:20,672
-I've got to go soon.
-Okay.

307
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,242
I'll stay a bit longer to look for Harune.

308
00:17:23,976 --> 00:17:24,977
Sure.

309
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:28,580
Finally, I'll be free from this heat.

310
00:17:28,647 --> 00:17:31,450
I'll finally be free of you, Ogoma.

311
00:17:31,517 --> 00:17:32,918
That comeback is lame.

312
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:35,754
Thanks for the coffee.

313
00:17:35,821 --> 00:17:36,822
Bye.

314
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:38,023
Take care.

315
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:39,091
I will.

316
00:17:55,374 --> 00:17:56,341
Hey! I'm back.

317
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:57,709
It has been a while!

318
00:17:57,776 --> 00:17:58,644
Long time no see.

319
00:18:10,556 --> 00:18:11,390
Good morning.

320
00:18:11,457 --> 00:18:12,624
Welcome back!

321
00:18:12,691 --> 00:18:13,659
Here, souvenirs.

322
00:18:13,725 --> 00:18:15,260
How was your summer vacation?

323
00:18:15,327 --> 00:18:16,862
Did you enjoy Tokyo?

324
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,164
I did…

325
00:18:19,231 --> 00:18:20,099
You got a girl there?

326
00:18:20,165 --> 00:18:21,867
No.

327
00:18:26,705 --> 00:18:29,908
Mr. Awashima, you really helped me out.

328
00:18:29,975 --> 00:18:31,210
They already found out.

329
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:32,377
Ogoma!

330
00:18:33,078 --> 00:18:35,314
Go quickly. Hurry!

331
00:18:36,915 --> 00:18:38,183
Did you really enjoy Tokyo?

332
00:18:42,221 --> 00:18:43,155
Okay.

333
00:18:46,058 --> 00:18:47,960
Excuse me.

334
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:50,963
Headquarters gave a strict warning.

335
00:18:51,763 --> 00:18:55,334
They said you chased Harune and obstructed
another team's investigation.

336
00:18:56,435 --> 00:19:00,572
Chief, did you already know
about those people's investigation?

337
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:05,677
We were ordered not to go
after the three missing people.

338
00:19:06,845 --> 00:19:11,884
It involved a secret investigation,
and we were told not to butt in.

339
00:19:11,950 --> 00:19:12,784
I see.

340
00:19:12,851 --> 00:19:15,287
Read the Investigation Rules properly!

341
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:19,758
In conducting an investigation,
do not go off on your own!

342
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,693
Obey your superiors' orders!

343
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:22,828
I'm sorry!

344
00:19:23,362 --> 00:19:25,864
Oh, and about Nikaido.

345
00:19:26,598 --> 00:19:28,934
Saruwatari is no longer a suspect.

346
00:19:32,905 --> 00:19:34,072
Really?

347
00:19:34,139 --> 00:19:37,743
New testimony came out,
so the investigation changed direction.

348
00:19:37,809 --> 00:19:41,480
The team whose investigation
you obstructed provided statements.

349
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:45,751
Then…

350
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:48,720
is the suspect now Tabatake?

351
00:19:49,588 --> 00:19:52,658
It's not a solo job.
HQ thinks there's a ringleader.

352
00:19:53,458 --> 00:19:54,359
A ringleader?

353
00:19:54,426 --> 00:19:58,163
They're starting to identify
who is behind all of this.

354
00:20:03,268 --> 00:20:05,971
They told you to return
to the investigation this Thursday!

355
00:20:07,139 --> 00:20:08,240
Yes, sir!

356
00:20:12,444 --> 00:20:13,712
Hello, miss.

357
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:15,914
Huh?

358
00:20:17,182 --> 00:20:18,016
Excuse me.

359
00:20:18,617 --> 00:20:20,118
-Yes?
-Where is Ms. Saruwatari?

360
00:20:20,185 --> 00:20:21,954
Oh, she was discharged.

361
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:23,755
-When?
-Earlier today.

362
00:20:23,822 --> 00:20:25,490
Got it. Thank you.

363
00:20:30,195 --> 00:20:32,030
I see you were discharged.

364
00:20:32,097 --> 00:20:33,165
I'm glad.

365
00:20:38,103 --> 00:20:40,138
Can we meet tomorrow?

366
00:20:44,977 --> 00:20:47,346
WE CAN. I NEED TO GO SOMEWHERE…

367
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:49,214
LIFE INSURANCE CONTRACT
TERUYUKI NIKAIDO

368
00:20:49,281 --> 00:20:50,382
Time is up.

369
00:20:50,449 --> 00:20:52,918
We must submit this report
to the insurance company.

370
00:20:52,985 --> 00:20:56,555
Let's wait for them to tell us
whether to continue looking for Harune.

371
00:20:56,622 --> 00:20:59,157
-How many days must I wait--
-I'll submit the report.

372
00:20:59,224 --> 00:21:00,359
Thanks for the hard work.

373
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:01,226
FINISHED

374
00:21:03,829 --> 00:21:05,797
Did you find the person
you were looking for?

375
00:21:06,398 --> 00:21:08,400
Well, Ogoma found his.

376
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:11,903
I'm heading back to Hokkaido to regroup.

377
00:21:12,571 --> 00:21:13,739
So you didn't find yours.

378
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:15,774
Unfortunately not.

379
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:28,320
Do you know what this is?

380
00:21:30,155 --> 00:21:31,790
I looked into lots of things, but…

381
00:21:33,025 --> 00:21:34,126
Where did you find it?

382
00:21:34,192 --> 00:21:35,994
It was found in someone's postbox.

383
00:21:37,329 --> 00:21:38,230
How about this?

384
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:40,299
That's only seven digits, though.

385
00:21:40,365 --> 00:21:43,969
This is a digital address that tells you
even the apartment number.

386
00:21:45,103 --> 00:21:46,872
Our company uses it often.

387
00:21:47,606 --> 00:21:49,107
There, okay…

388
00:21:49,174 --> 00:21:50,509
An address?

389
00:21:51,043 --> 00:21:53,312
-What about the last four digits--
-An address.

390
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:56,315
HOSHIMINO HEIGHTS 307
AOMINE WARD, YOKOHAMA, KANAGAWA

391
00:22:02,087 --> 00:22:03,388
Sorry to call you here--

392
00:22:03,455 --> 00:22:05,724
Hoshimino 4-3-12, we've arrived.

393
00:22:06,758 --> 00:22:08,093
You should have told me earlier!

394
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:11,430
Look, we weren't on good terms earlier.

395
00:22:12,064 --> 00:22:12,931
Is it here?

396
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,733
Who lives here?

397
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,834
An illegal sublet.

398
00:22:15,901 --> 00:22:17,369
They take guests without registering.

399
00:22:17,436 --> 00:22:18,603
Sublet?

400
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:22,307
-What's the apartment number?
-It's 307.

401
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:33,185
The last four digits.

402
00:22:34,986 --> 00:22:37,055
Nine, four, seven, one.

403
00:22:39,658 --> 00:22:40,692
Hey!

404
00:22:41,293 --> 00:22:42,361
Wait!

405
00:22:42,427 --> 00:22:43,528
I don't know anything!

406
00:22:43,595 --> 00:22:46,298
I'm just a part-timer!
They hired me as a courier!

407
00:22:48,433 --> 00:22:49,434
Here?

408
00:22:53,004 --> 00:22:54,239
Contact Narcotics.

409
00:22:54,306 --> 00:22:55,273
Okay.

410
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,677
Excuse me.

411
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:00,645
Stay there.

412
00:23:01,179 --> 00:23:02,214
Don't come in.

413
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:03,248
Okay.

414
00:23:07,085 --> 00:23:08,820
Something has been bugging me.

415
00:23:10,956 --> 00:23:12,958
I'm older than you, right?

416
00:23:21,032 --> 00:23:23,268
-So what?
-Nothing.

417
00:23:24,403 --> 00:23:26,037
Hello. Sorry to bother you.

418
00:23:26,104 --> 00:23:26,972
I'm just a part-timer!

419
00:23:27,038 --> 00:23:30,642
It seems they changed locations
for each deal, with digital addresses.

420
00:23:30,709 --> 00:23:31,610
I'll request backup.

421
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,350
Should I help?

422
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:48,393
-Hold this.
-Okay.

423
00:23:52,464 --> 00:23:53,532
Light up where I'm looking!

424
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:56,067
Yes, sorry. Here.

425
00:23:57,402 --> 00:23:58,303
Whoa.

426
00:23:59,237 --> 00:24:00,806
That Shikara cop…

427
00:24:01,907 --> 00:24:03,141
You mean Ogoma?

428
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:04,376
What kind of guy is he?

429
00:24:04,976 --> 00:24:06,812
That's a hard question to answer.

430
00:24:07,479 --> 00:24:08,914
His strengths and weaknesses?

431
00:24:10,515 --> 00:24:13,452
His strength lies in his persistence.

432
00:24:14,052 --> 00:24:15,720
Rather than shallow justice,

433
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:18,023
it's a better quality
for detectives to have.

434
00:24:18,089 --> 00:24:19,124
His weakness?

435
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:21,393
He's frighteningly impulsive.

436
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:25,363
But with a good boss, he'll grow.
Probably.

437
00:24:36,775 --> 00:24:38,643
Send a Forensics team here.

438
00:24:40,946 --> 00:24:42,614
What money is this?

439
00:24:43,849 --> 00:24:46,818
If I learn where Harune went,
I'll tell you.

440
00:24:46,885 --> 00:24:47,986
Really?

441
00:24:49,921 --> 00:24:51,756
Go back to that small town.

442
00:24:53,225 --> 00:24:54,192
Okay.

443
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:05,403
The police stopped calling me.

444
00:25:05,470 --> 00:25:08,039
It's all thanks to you, Ogoma. Thank you.

445
00:25:08,573 --> 00:25:11,543
You sure you don't mind
coming with me here?

446
00:25:11,610 --> 00:25:12,544
It's fine.

447
00:25:13,111 --> 00:25:15,413
I'm from this town too.

448
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:16,815
Trainee teachers like me

449
00:25:16,882 --> 00:25:19,885
usually teach at the very school
they graduated from.

450
00:25:19,951 --> 00:25:22,854
Huh? So we went to the same middle school?

451
00:25:22,921 --> 00:25:25,824
Was your friend at the same school too?

452
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:28,026
Yes. He was three years older.

453
00:25:28,093 --> 00:25:30,896
And our houses were next to each other.

454
00:25:32,097 --> 00:25:34,866
Do you come here
to pay respects every year?

455
00:25:38,303 --> 00:25:39,204
Tetsu!

456
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:40,939
I'm here!

457
00:25:41,606 --> 00:25:43,909
Hey, Tetsu, please! Wake up!

458
00:25:44,476 --> 00:25:46,077
Please, don't die!

459
00:25:47,178 --> 00:25:48,813
Don't die!

460
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:51,116
Please!

461
00:25:53,184 --> 00:25:54,252
Don't die…

462
00:25:55,387 --> 00:25:59,591
My parents weren't around often.

463
00:26:01,359 --> 00:26:05,363
Whenever I got home,
the house was always dark and empty.

464
00:26:07,198 --> 00:26:08,099
So,

465
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:11,970
Tetsu always told me to come to his house.

466
00:26:14,272 --> 00:26:16,474
I basically lived there.

467
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:24,516
I would eat meals at his place.

468
00:26:28,253 --> 00:26:30,455
Slept on a futon at his place.

469
00:26:32,123 --> 00:26:33,925
He wasn't a friend anymore.

470
00:26:33,992 --> 00:26:35,360
He was basically family to you.

471
00:26:40,198 --> 00:26:44,569
I probably talked with Tetsu
more than I talked to my parents.

472
00:26:47,305 --> 00:26:51,476
We only ever talked
about dumb stuff though.

473
00:26:57,048 --> 00:27:02,053
If an adult like you
had come into our lives earlier…

474
00:27:07,425 --> 00:27:10,228
maybe Tetsu would still be alive.

475
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:20,071
I wasn't really an adult either.

476
00:27:21,106 --> 00:27:22,407
I was still in university.

477
00:27:25,710 --> 00:27:27,679
You looked like an adult to me.

478
00:27:28,713 --> 00:27:30,081
I'll come back, Tetsu.

479
00:27:32,751 --> 00:27:36,888
I wasn't even sure
if I could be a teacher.

480
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:40,859
Last year, the school closed down.
Did you know that?

481
00:27:40,925 --> 00:27:41,793
What?

482
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:45,130
Not enough kids in town anymore.

483
00:27:45,196 --> 00:27:46,731
Even in my time, there weren't many.

484
00:27:46,798 --> 00:27:47,632
Ogoma.

485
00:27:47,699 --> 00:27:48,767
When I climb mountains,

486
00:27:48,833 --> 00:27:52,137
I sometimes meet kids
whom I taught back then.

487
00:27:52,203 --> 00:27:55,974
They say the school hike
inspired them to start climbing.

488
00:27:57,208 --> 00:27:59,277
So school events do have meaning.

489
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:00,779
Of course they do.

490
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:02,080
I always skipped them.

491
00:28:02,147 --> 00:28:03,248
Do you even go to work?

492
00:28:03,314 --> 00:28:04,616
I skip it too…

493
00:28:05,216 --> 00:28:09,187
I know. Someday you'll be a legendary cop.

494
00:28:09,254 --> 00:28:10,822
Do you mean that in a good way?

495
00:28:10,889 --> 00:28:11,990
Of course.

496
00:28:15,026 --> 00:28:16,294
Brings back memories, huh?

497
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:18,463
It sure does.

498
00:28:20,498 --> 00:28:22,000
It's hot.

499
00:28:22,067 --> 00:28:22,901
Yes.

500
00:28:24,402 --> 00:28:25,236
This is my seat.

501
00:28:31,743 --> 00:28:32,410
Ogoma.

502
00:28:33,244 --> 00:28:35,814
I need you to help me
with something after school.

503
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:41,453
What?

504
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:45,757
I have a problem.

505
00:28:46,624 --> 00:28:47,559
Yeah?

506
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:52,197
Seeing dead bodies
really takes a toll on me.

507
00:28:54,833 --> 00:28:57,569
-Sorry for talking about this.
-It's fine.

508
00:28:58,737 --> 00:28:59,671
May I continue?

509
00:29:00,205 --> 00:29:01,239
Of course.

510
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:04,809
I was assigned to the criminal section.

511
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:08,513
It investigates murders and robberies.

512
00:29:10,315 --> 00:29:13,651
But my jurisdiction is peaceful.
Basically zero murders.

513
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:18,523
Sometimes, elderly people die of old age,
but experienced officers handle it.

514
00:29:19,390 --> 00:29:22,827
This case was my first time at a scene.

515
00:29:26,164 --> 00:29:30,735
Can someone like me
ever become a legendary cop?

516
00:29:36,508 --> 00:29:41,246
Back then, you could have run away.

517
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:46,017
To avoid being involved, you could
have pretended not to know anything.

518
00:29:48,319 --> 00:29:49,354
But…

519
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:52,290
you chose not to run away.

520
00:29:52,957 --> 00:29:56,961
You called an ambulance
and tried to save Tetsu.

521
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:02,400
Don't think that you could have done more.

522
00:30:06,237 --> 00:30:09,207
You did everything you could.

523
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:12,610
You did the right thing.

524
00:30:31,863 --> 00:30:35,166
If one of your students is involved
in anything dangerous, please tell me.

525
00:30:36,267 --> 00:30:38,903
I'll do my best to stop them.

526
00:30:43,241 --> 00:30:46,477
My students are all good kids.

527
00:30:46,978 --> 00:30:51,783
But if one of them ever becomes like that,
please help me out.

528
00:30:52,884 --> 00:30:53,952
Yes.

529
00:30:55,186 --> 00:30:56,221
I'm counting on you.

530
00:30:56,955 --> 00:30:58,056
Leave it to me.

531
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:01,092
Pass the shuttlecock!

532
00:31:01,159 --> 00:31:02,594
Yes!

533
00:31:02,660 --> 00:31:04,128
Focus!

534
00:31:05,129 --> 00:31:06,431
Make them all count!

535
00:31:06,998 --> 00:31:09,434
Tomorrow, five reps, ten sets.

536
00:31:09,500 --> 00:31:10,768
What?

537
00:31:10,835 --> 00:31:11,903
Don't "what" me.

538
00:31:11,970 --> 00:31:14,772
I'll increase it
to ten reps, ten sets, you know.

539
00:31:15,673 --> 00:31:17,709
That's when you should go, "what"!

540
00:31:19,043 --> 00:31:20,411
Thank you very much.

541
00:31:21,112 --> 00:31:23,147
Thank you very much.

542
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:24,282
Tidy up!

543
00:31:24,349 --> 00:31:25,516
Yes!

544
00:31:30,021 --> 00:31:31,422
Ms. Saruwatari.

545
00:31:32,390 --> 00:31:34,325
I need your advice on something.

546
00:31:35,927 --> 00:31:37,762
It was found in our club room.

547
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:40,565
A second-year picked it up
and brought it in.

548
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:44,302
None of the club members recognize it.

549
00:31:46,137 --> 00:31:49,073
We got a notice last year
from the Board of Education, right?

550
00:31:49,140 --> 00:31:50,141
Yes.

551
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:52,343
They were warning us about a drug.

552
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:54,279
SAMPLE PHOTO

553
00:31:54,345 --> 00:31:55,713
"CAN-d."

554
00:31:57,949 --> 00:31:59,684
Have you told the principal?

555
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:02,420
Yes, but he hasn't answered yet.

556
00:32:03,054 --> 00:32:05,556
The club members
are suspecting each other,

557
00:32:05,623 --> 00:32:06,491
and things are tense.

558
00:32:06,557 --> 00:32:07,625
Calm down.

559
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:09,260
Maybe this is just a supplement.

560
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:10,828
What should we do?

561
00:32:14,666 --> 00:32:16,901
I'll try a component analysis.

562
00:32:16,968 --> 00:32:19,971
Until the result comes out,
don't blame anyone.

563
00:32:20,038 --> 00:32:21,673
You can have it analyzed?

564
00:32:23,541 --> 00:32:26,277
I know someone who can.

565
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:37,422
OGOMA - SHIKARA STATION

566
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:52,837
Huh? Are you going somewhere?
Want to go together?

567
00:32:54,005 --> 00:32:56,808
You go ahead first.
You have a flight, right?

568
00:32:59,177 --> 00:33:02,580
Oh, thank you for helping me
with that digital address.

569
00:33:05,783 --> 00:33:07,852
See you. And thanks again.

570
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:16,294
Yes?

571
00:33:16,361 --> 00:33:18,296
Hello! You have a parcel!

572
00:33:18,363 --> 00:33:19,797
Please wait a bit.

573
00:33:21,132 --> 00:33:22,066
Oh, sorry!

574
00:33:22,133 --> 00:33:23,568
It's heavy, please be careful.

575
00:33:23,634 --> 00:33:24,869
Okay.

576
00:33:25,436 --> 00:33:26,304
Yes.

577
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,072
Sorry, Akane, may I?

578
00:33:28,139 --> 00:33:29,007
Sure.

579
00:33:29,841 --> 00:33:31,509
It's from Ogoma.

580
00:33:44,389 --> 00:33:46,324
Wow!

581
00:33:46,924 --> 00:33:48,292
Huh?

582
00:33:49,060 --> 00:33:50,762
Amazing.

583
00:33:51,462 --> 00:33:53,531
How do you even eat this?

584
00:33:53,598 --> 00:33:55,366
You plan to eat it alone?

585
00:33:56,401 --> 00:33:59,037
He sent it to both you and me.

586
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:01,773
But you're leaving, right?

587
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:05,676
I'll change to another flight.

588
00:34:06,978 --> 00:34:09,280
Is this for a paella?

589
00:34:09,914 --> 00:34:13,785
What are you saying? I'm sure
you grill this with salt and butter.

590
00:34:13,851 --> 00:34:14,819
What?

591
00:34:21,492 --> 00:34:22,593
Have you been already?

592
00:34:22,660 --> 00:34:23,494
What?

593
00:34:24,328 --> 00:34:25,830
To Minori's grave.

594
00:34:26,764 --> 00:34:28,366
I plan to go now.

595
00:34:30,268 --> 00:34:31,202
I see.

596
00:34:36,874 --> 00:34:38,309
Maybe I'll go too.

597
00:34:46,584 --> 00:34:49,954
When you come back, let's talk a bit.

598
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:52,657
About what we do from now on.

599
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:55,726
Will you come back to me,

600
00:34:56,627 --> 00:34:58,229
or do we keep living separately?

601
00:35:01,966 --> 00:35:02,900
Sure.

602
00:35:04,502 --> 00:35:05,603
Let's do that.

603
00:35:27,225 --> 00:35:29,127
Which do you want to eat first?

604
00:35:32,196 --> 00:35:33,164
Scallops?

605
00:35:41,439 --> 00:35:44,041
-Welcome. Please wait there.
-Hello. Okay!

606
00:35:51,048 --> 00:35:52,316
You're that missing person!

607
00:35:52,383 --> 00:35:55,453
Cut it out already.

608
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:57,755
How long have you been here?

609
00:35:57,822 --> 00:35:59,023
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

610
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:02,260
-I'm Nobori. I have a reservation.
-Mr. Nobori, I'll show you to your seat.

611
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:03,161
Okay.

612
00:36:03,961 --> 00:36:05,096
Hey!

613
00:36:07,565 --> 00:36:08,533
Are you a kid?

614
00:36:09,534 --> 00:36:10,368
You drove here?

615
00:36:10,434 --> 00:36:12,670
Why would I? We're going to drink, right?

616
00:36:12,737 --> 00:36:13,771
Go ahead then.

617
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:16,207
Sorry I couldn't go on the cleaning trek.

618
00:36:16,807 --> 00:36:19,577
Everyone was saying it's rare
for you to miss a trip.

619
00:36:19,644 --> 00:36:23,080
It's really pathetic. I got careless.

620
00:36:23,147 --> 00:36:24,615
-Thank you.
-Looks good.

621
00:36:25,216 --> 00:36:26,684
What are you getting?

622
00:36:29,086 --> 00:36:30,087
Napolitan pasta.

623
00:36:30,154 --> 00:36:34,225
I get it. I'm torn
between curry and the Napolitan.

624
00:36:34,292 --> 00:36:37,161
I don't know which to pick. Which one?

625
00:36:37,228 --> 00:36:38,196
I'll give you half.

626
00:36:38,262 --> 00:36:39,997
Really? Then I'll take it.

627
00:36:40,064 --> 00:36:42,166
-One Napolitan and one curry.
-Yes.

628
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:43,935
-Yes, and two beers.
-Yes.

629
00:36:44,001 --> 00:36:45,770
-Thank you.
-Coming right up.

630
00:36:47,338 --> 00:36:48,272
So…

631
00:36:50,675 --> 00:36:52,443
Will we talk first?

632
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:55,179
-Or after the meal?
-Let's talk first.

633
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,081
Okay.

634
00:36:58,916 --> 00:37:02,086
Can you keep this a secret?

635
00:37:04,188 --> 00:37:05,223
What's wrong?

636
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:09,093
What?

637
00:37:19,270 --> 00:37:20,238
This.

638
00:37:20,805 --> 00:37:22,773
I want to know what this is.

639
00:37:24,275 --> 00:37:25,276
What is it?

640
00:37:27,878 --> 00:37:28,846
Huh?

641
00:37:30,181 --> 00:37:31,249
Keep it there.

642
00:37:33,251 --> 00:37:35,019
That's what I want to find out.

643
00:37:36,988 --> 00:37:38,956
-Can I open it?
-Yes.

644
00:37:44,295 --> 00:37:47,965
No matter the results,
you mustn't tell anyone but me.

645
00:37:51,402 --> 00:37:52,837
Welcome back.

646
00:37:53,404 --> 00:37:55,406
Huh? Got a new look?

647
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:56,974
Thanks.

648
00:37:57,942 --> 00:38:00,678
The seafood you sent was great.
Especially the scallops.

649
00:38:01,312 --> 00:38:02,480
They were sent fresh that morning.

650
00:38:02,546 --> 00:38:07,051
Akane and I ate our fill.

651
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:18,296
I'm glad Akane liked it.

652
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:22,266
Oh, what about Harune?

653
00:38:23,501 --> 00:38:25,436
I haven't found her.

654
00:38:25,936 --> 00:38:27,905
Then why did you come back?

655
00:38:27,972 --> 00:38:31,042
Time ran out, I had to submit the report.

656
00:38:31,108 --> 00:38:32,810
And I want to help with Nono's matter.

657
00:38:38,616 --> 00:38:42,086
Anyway, I got an appointment
with Dr. Yoshino.

658
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:43,721
Ogoma, want to come with me?

659
00:38:44,622 --> 00:38:47,158
The chief told me not to do
any unnecessary investigating.

660
00:38:47,725 --> 00:38:50,661
Maybe we can learn
Ms. Tabatake's cash flow.

661
00:38:51,429 --> 00:38:53,097
Is that unnecessary?

662
00:38:54,065 --> 00:38:58,569
I think the one in the wrong here
is the police, not you.

663
00:39:04,642 --> 00:39:06,177
Let's go talk to him.

664
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:09,013
Sorry to keep you waiting. I've been busy.

665
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:12,350
We came to talk to you on behalf of Chika.

666
00:39:12,416 --> 00:39:14,385
Here's the consent form.

667
00:39:14,452 --> 00:39:16,220
It's about Nono's medical costs, right?

668
00:39:17,021 --> 00:39:18,656
Chika called me this morning.

669
00:39:19,757 --> 00:39:21,759
You mind if I eat while we talk?

670
00:39:21,826 --> 00:39:24,829
Of course not. Sorry for bothering you.

671
00:39:28,299 --> 00:39:31,969
Ms. Tabatake's death
was truly regrettable.

672
00:39:35,106 --> 00:39:36,841
How is Nono?

673
00:39:36,907 --> 00:39:38,642
She still has a low fever.

674
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:42,413
Her illness?
I heard gene therapy might help.

675
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:45,649
As pretreatment,
we're giving her chemotherapy drugs.

676
00:39:46,183 --> 00:39:48,152
The therapy can be quite taxing.

677
00:39:50,821 --> 00:39:56,460
Chika gave us this.
Nono's medical costs are listed here.

678
00:39:56,527 --> 00:39:58,863
They're quite high.

679
00:39:58,929 --> 00:40:01,999
Some months cost over a million yen.

680
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:05,169
Is this correct?

681
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,303
It is.

682
00:40:07,772 --> 00:40:09,807
Why does it cost this much?

683
00:40:09,874 --> 00:40:13,210
The medicine prescribed for her
is unapproved in Japan,

684
00:40:13,944 --> 00:40:15,312
so it's out-of-pocket.

685
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:17,915
Insurance doesn't apply.

686
00:40:19,283 --> 00:40:22,186
Conventional medication
had no effect on her anymore.

687
00:40:23,387 --> 00:40:25,289
So you have to use this drug?

688
00:40:27,024 --> 00:40:32,163
It costs more than 600,000 yen a month.

689
00:40:32,229 --> 00:40:33,964
Each case is different.

690
00:40:34,031 --> 00:40:36,934
But in this specific case,
prescribing a non-insured drug

691
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:40,070
makes other medical fees
out-of-pocket too. All of it.

692
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:43,340
Subsidy programs can't be used either.

693
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:49,413
Do you know how Ms. Tabatake
paid this astronomical amount?

694
00:40:50,181 --> 00:40:51,315
No.

695
00:40:51,382 --> 00:40:53,784
A normal person
can't earn this much a month.

696
00:40:54,318 --> 00:40:58,456
For Nono's comfort, Ms. Tabatake chose
this drug for the treatment.

697
00:41:00,191 --> 00:41:04,094
If the family can afford it,
we doctors will respect their wishes.

698
00:41:04,728 --> 00:41:08,566
What happens with Nono's
medication from now on?

699
00:41:09,667 --> 00:41:12,236
Chika said it will be paid
from Ms. Tabatake's savings.

700
00:41:14,405 --> 00:41:16,674
Do you know how much her savings are?

701
00:41:21,779 --> 00:41:23,614
They won't last six months.

702
00:41:23,681 --> 00:41:25,449
At most, four months.

703
00:41:25,983 --> 00:41:28,252
Only four months, I see.

704
00:41:28,819 --> 00:41:32,990
If Ms. Tabatake's life insurance is paid,
they can manage.

705
00:41:33,657 --> 00:41:36,827
They can buy time
until gene therapy is possible.

706
00:41:36,894 --> 00:41:39,096
But Ms. Tabatake is surely guilty.

707
00:41:39,663 --> 00:41:42,566
Her motive for needing money is clear.

708
00:41:42,633 --> 00:41:44,702
You can't be certain she is guilty yet!

709
00:41:44,768 --> 00:41:47,104
We also don't know why she killed herself.

710
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:51,442
Don't take crime lightly.

711
00:41:51,976 --> 00:41:54,345
Once an ordinary person
commits a crime, in the end--

712
00:41:54,411 --> 00:41:56,347
Don't keep saying
"crime this, crime that."

713
00:41:56,881 --> 00:42:00,918
When Ms. Aya was wrongly suspected,
you were so angry.

714
00:42:01,785 --> 00:42:03,220
What's your problem?!

715
00:42:05,222 --> 00:42:07,958
You are doing all this for Nono, right?

716
00:42:08,759 --> 00:42:10,160
I just want the money.

717
00:42:14,365 --> 00:42:15,900
I won't give up.

718
00:42:17,034 --> 00:42:21,205
I'll do everything I can
so that the life insurance can be paid.

719
00:42:21,939 --> 00:42:24,942
Even if the chance is 0.00001%.

720
00:42:26,944 --> 00:42:29,046
You're not thinking of doing
something shady, are you?

721
00:42:29,113 --> 00:42:30,147
Shady?

722
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:31,081
Yes.

723
00:42:31,682 --> 00:42:33,617
"Anything you can." What is that?

724
00:42:33,684 --> 00:42:35,252
Something illegal?

725
00:42:36,253 --> 00:42:38,355
No way.

726
00:42:38,422 --> 00:42:39,523
Really?

727
00:42:50,434 --> 00:42:52,169
I'll listen to your breathing.

728
00:42:56,473 --> 00:42:57,808
I'm going to check your eyes.

729
00:42:59,376 --> 00:43:00,811
I'm going to give her oxygen.

730
00:43:01,445 --> 00:43:02,880
I'm going to give you oxygen, okay?

731
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:04,748
You'll feel better soon.

732
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:10,020
Hang in there.

733
00:43:11,855 --> 00:43:12,957
Hang in there.

734
00:43:19,129 --> 00:43:20,064
You have a delivery!

735
00:43:20,130 --> 00:43:21,365
Oh, thank you.

736
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:22,700
What is it?

737
00:43:22,766 --> 00:43:24,602
This is for Mommy.

738
00:43:24,668 --> 00:43:26,103
Let me open it!

739
00:43:26,170 --> 00:43:27,738
Be careful.

740
00:43:29,239 --> 00:43:30,307
Here you go!

741
00:43:30,374 --> 00:43:31,375
Thank you.

742
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:32,576
And this too.

743
00:43:32,643 --> 00:43:33,577
Thanks.

744
00:43:33,644 --> 00:43:36,013
Thank you for your call. I'm Shimizu.

745
00:43:36,080 --> 00:43:38,749
Is this notebook my sister's?

746
00:43:39,383 --> 00:43:40,618
We believe so.

747
00:43:41,218 --> 00:43:42,820
Nono said it was her mom's.

748
00:43:43,887 --> 00:43:47,257
LIFE INSURANCE CONTRACT

749
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:56,634
About the notebook…

750
00:43:56,700 --> 00:43:58,535
Please don't tell anyone about it.

751
00:43:58,602 --> 00:44:00,070
You hiding something from me?

752
00:44:00,137 --> 00:44:02,473
-You should consult the police.
-Hey!

753
00:44:02,539 --> 00:44:04,375
Stay with me! Ogoma!

754
00:44:04,441 --> 00:44:05,409
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
